Doordash problem and needs:
- people want food from places that dont deliver
- restaurants want more customers, but cant afford to hire drivers all the time
- drivers want flexible income without full time commitment

Doordash:
- shared delivery network serving all three groups
- cost of operations is spread across the orders

3-sided marketplace:
- Consumer
- Merchant
- Dasher

Merchants prefer to be on Doordash rather than hiring drivers, as that turns out to be expensive.

Deeper goal: building the local commerce platform. not just food, but anything that can be delivered from a local business. Logistics layer of physical world

Business operation:
- consumer places the order -> merchant receives the order -> dispatch a dasher -> dasher picks up and delivers -> post delivery consumer can rate or ask for help

Revenue streams:
- Commission from merchants: Merchants pay DoorDash a percentage of every order. largest revenue source
- Delivery and service fees: consumers pay delivery and service fee. 
- Dashpass: subscription product, free delivery + reduced fees
- Advertising: Merchants pay to appear higher in search results or promotional placements
- Dashmart: own dark stores, margin on customers buying from here

Dasher management:
- independent contractors, not employers
- dynamic pricing to incentivize dashers to work during high demand periods
- batching where dahsers pick from multiple restaurants. improves cost and earnings for dasher, but longer time for consumer. so tradeoff to manage

DoorDash became popular by focusing on suburban markets which competitors deprioritized

Key Metrics:
- Most important: Gross Order Value: total $ value of orders placed on platform
      (why dont we we include other revenue drivers here?)
- GOV = #Orders*Average Order Value

Consumer Metrics:
- MAU/DAU for platform health
- Order frequency + retention for engagement, habit formation and acquistion quality
- AOV: Revenue per transaction
- DashPass attach rate
- Churn rate
- LTV

Merchant Metrics:
- % of local restaurants available
- monthly merchant volume
- merchant retention
- order volume per merchant
- fulfillment rate: % of orders accepted vs cancelled

Dasher metrics:
- Dasher utilization: % of dashing time spten on active deliveries -> unit economics
- earnings per hour-> satisfaction
- deliveries per hour -> throughput

Platform metrics:
- Delivery time end to end
- % of deliveries within estimated window
- % of orders that dont complete
- take rate: monetization efficiency
- CM: GOV - (Dasher pay+merchat take+ refunds)

